# moment kind=street3d cam=worm near=1.1 traffic=34 art="$17|a whole day?" artfx=stack artAt=-0.25 artOut=5.5 fg=wires dur=6.5 trans=cut
Guess what one full day in Vietnam costs.
Breakfast. Coffee. Rides. Two meals, a beer, and a bed.
# talk place=oldquarter host=linh pose=present big="REAL PRICES" shots="WS|MS|CU" dur=12 trans=cut
In the next five minutes: every price from one ordinary day, checked this month.
Three budgets, from backpacker to comfortable.
And the one habit that quietly makes everything cost four times more.
# chapter num=1 text="Morning" dur=3 trans=circles trans=whip
Chapter one. Morning.
# price place=sidewalk hero=dave seller=banhmi hold=banhmi item="bánh mì" vnd="25.000 ₫" usd="$1" checked="Oct 2026" react=yummy art="25.000 ₫|breakfast" artfx=count artAt=1.4 shots="MS|CU" dur=8 trans=cut
Breakfast is a bánh mì from a cart: twenty-five thousand dong, about *one dollar*.
The same sandwich inside a café with air conditioning? Fifty to sixty.
# countdown n=2 text="Cà phê đen đá" sub="20.000 ₫ · ≈ $0.80" prop=caphe size=1.6 bg=#17224d dur=7 trans=iris
Iced black coffee on a plastic stool: twenty thousand.
A specialty café charges fifty to ninety for the same beans.
# chapter num=2 text="Getting around" dur=3 trans=whip
Chapter two. Getting around.
# price place=oldquarter hero=dave seller=xeom item="GrabBike ride" vnd="30.000 ₫" usd="$1.15" checked="Oct 2026" art="30.000 ₫|GrabBike across town" artfx=count artAt=1.4 shots="MS|CU" dur=8 trans=cut
A GrabBike across the centre is twenty to fifty thousand. Call it thirty.
A car for the same trip: fifty to a hundred and twenty.
# steps place=oldquarter title="THE AIRPORT RULE" items="Book the car in the app|Airport to the centre: 200–280k ₫|Never take the first kerb offer" icons="phone|money|backpack" host=linh shots="MS|CU" dur=11 trans=cut
The airport is where most people lose money on day one.
In the app, airport to the centre runs two hundred to two hundred and eighty thousand.
At the kerb, the first price is usually double.
# chapter num=3 text="Midday" dur=3 trans=iris trans=whip
Chapter three. Midday.
# price place=sidewalk hero=dave seller=cophovn hold=pho item="phở bò" vnd="45.000 ₫" usd="$1.80" checked="Oct 2026" react=yummy art="45.000 ₫|lunch" artfx=count artAt=1.4 shots="MS|CU" dur=8 trans=circles
Lunch is phở: forty to fifty-five thousand in Hà Nội, a little more in Sài Gòn.
# stat value=120000 from=0 suffix=" ₫" label="spent before noon · about $4.60" bg=#17224d dur=6 trans=ink
By noon you've spent a hundred and twenty thousand. Four dollars sixty.
# countdown n=5 text="Museum ticket" sub="40.000 ₫ · ≈ $1.55" prop=ticket size=1.6 bg=#17224d dur=6 trans=whip
Most museums cost forty thousand. A viewing deck is two hundred.
# chapter num=4 text="Night" dur=3 trans=whip
Chapter four. Night.
# social place=night_market hero=dave host=xeom toasts=2 cheer="MỘT, HAI, BA… DZÔ!" fg=lanterns shots="MS|CU" dur=9 trans=tear art="10.000 ₫|a glass of bia hơi" artfx=count artAt=1.8 artY=.14 artX=.3
Bia hơi is brewed in the morning and gone by night. Seven to fifteen thousand a glass.
Two glasses still costs less than half a dollar.
# price place=sidewalk hero=dave seller=cophovn hold=buncha item="bún chả" vnd="55.000 ₫" usd="$2.10" checked="Oct 2026" react=happy art="55.000 ₫|dinner" artfx=count artAt=1.4 shots="CU|MS" dur=8 trans=fgwipe
Dinner is bún chả over coals: forty-five to sixty-five thousand.
# chapter num=5 text="The bed" dur=3 trans=fgwipe trans=whip
Chapter five. The bed.
# dialogue a=dave b=hostel place=oldquarter voiceA=am_puck voiceB=am_fenrir act="hostel:point" lines="a:thinking:And a bed for tonight?|b:happy:Dorm. Two hundred thousand.|a:shocked:…Eight dollars?|b:smug:With breakfast."
# compare leftTitle="DORM BED" rightTitle="3-STAR HOTEL" left=dave right=linh leftPrice="200.000 ₫;$8;per night, breakfast in" rightPrice="900.000 ₫;$35;per night" checked="Oct 2026" shots="WS|CU" dur=10 trans=inkbleed
A dorm bed is a hundred to three hundred thousand.
A private room starts around three hundred, and a three-star hotel runs seven hundred and fifty thousand upward.
# moment kind=pass hero=dave place=hagiang time=sunset dur=9 art="155.000 ₫|a bed in Hà Giang · dinner included" artfx=count artAt=1.6 trans=cut
And those are city prices.
Up in Hà Giang, a homestay bed is about a hundred and fifty-five thousand.
Dinner usually comes with it.
# chapter num=6 text="The costs nobody lists" dur=4.5 trans=whip
Chapter six. The costs nobody puts in a daily budget.
# list place=oldquarter host=linh title="ONCE, NOT DAILY" items="Local SIM · 100–300k ₫ a month|Motorbike rental · 100–250k ₫ a day|Sleeper bus · 390–650k ₫ a night|Domestic flight · 1–2M ₫" shots="MS|CU" dur=19 trans=cut
A local SIM is a hundred to three hundred thousand for a month of data.
Renting a motorbike is a hundred to two hundred and fifty thousand a day.
An overnight sleeper bus is fifteen to twenty-five dollars, and it saves you a hotel night.
A domestic flight booked three weeks ahead is forty to eighty dollars.
# route stops="hanoi,ninhbinh,hue,hoian" stats="2,1M ₫;transport for the whole route|6 nights;dorms and homestays" hero=dave vehicle=moto dur=14 trans=cut
So a week from Hà Nội down to Hội An, by bus and one short flight, moves you for around two million dong.
That's eighty dollars of travel for six nights of the trip.
# moment kind=street3d cam=bird traffic=28 shots="WS|CU" dur=7 art="x3|what tourists pay" artfx=stamp artAt=1.4 trans=cut
Here's the pattern underneath all of it.
Vietnam has two price lists, and nobody tells you which one you're reading.
# budget title="ONE ORDINARY DAY" items="Bánh mì;25k|Coffee;20k|GrabBike;30k|Phở;45k|Museum;40k|Bia hơi ×2;20k|Bún chả;55k|Dorm bed;200k" total="435.000 ₫" usd="≈ $17" checked="Oct 2026" dur=12 drop=1.0 art="435.000 ₫|a whole day · ≈ $17" artfx=slam artAt=1.2 trans=cut
Back to the day. Add the eight prices up.
Four hundred and thirty-five thousand dong.
About *seventeen dollars* for the whole day.
# compare leftTitle="STREET CAFÉ" rightTitle="TOURIST CAFÉ" left=barista right=dave leftPrice="20.000 ₫;$0.80;cà phê đen đá" rightPrice="90.000 ₫;$3.50;same coffee, nicer chair" checked="Oct 2026" shots="WS|CU" dur=10 trans=cut
Now the habit that breaks the budget.
The same iced coffee, fifty metres away, costs ninety thousand.
Four times the price. For the chair.
# quiz place=cafe_giang q="Which costs more in Hà Nội?" options="A western breakfast|Four bowls of phở|They're the same" answer=1 reveal=6 dur=11 trans=cut
Quick one. Which costs more in Hà Nội?
A western breakfast in a tourist café…
or four bowls of phở?
The breakfast. Usually by a long way.
# talk place=cafe_giang host=linh pose=present big="2 PRICE LISTS" shots="WS|MS|CU" dur=11 trans=inkbleed
This is the whole trick. There is a street price and a visitor price, and they sit side by side.
Nobody is cheating you. You're just standing in the wrong queue.
# list place=oldquarter host=linh title="THREE BUDGETS A DAY" items="Backpacker · 350k ₫ ≈ $13|Comfortable · 900k ₫ ≈ $35|Easy · 2,5M ₫ ≈ $95|!Tourist-priced everything: 3× more" dur=14 trans=cut
So three budgets. Thirteen dollars if you sleep in dorms and eat on the street.
Thirty-five with a private room and a sit-down dinner.
Ninety-five if you want a pool and taxis everywhere.
# steps place=oldquarter title="DON'T OVERPAY" items="Eat where the stools are already full|Agree the price before you get on|Book rides in the app, not at the kerb" icons="banhmi|money|phone" host=linh shots="MS|CU" dur=11
Three rules, and honestly they're the whole video.
Eat where the plastic stools are already full.
Agree a price before you get on anything.
And book rides in the app, not at the kerb.
